  "body": "## Why\nRuntime logs exposed multiple reasons historical opportunities were being starved:\n\n1. Bot 3 had 145 price-eligible DISCOVERED listings and 56 S25 target matches, but backend returned `may start 0 new negotiations`. Capacity was reserving every theoretical future step of every active conversation, so a few active negotiations could consume the entire theoretical budget even though those future actions had not happened.\n2. Bot 4 found a clear S11 Ultra candidate by URL, but mandatory final item-page verification failed because the expected Vinted h1 layout did not appear in time.\n3. Historical target mismatches stayed DISCOVERED forever, repeatedly polluting the backlog.\n4. The runtime log also exposed `Galaxy S25 Edge` being accepted as plain `Galaxy S25`.\n\n## Changes\n- negotiation capacity now reflects actual remaining daily action quota instead of pre-reserving hypothetical future steps\n- configured `dailyNegotiationBudget` is the actual per-bot daily limit for real price actions (first offers + next steps), capped at 25\n- future steps consume quota only when they are actually about to be sent\n- frontend copy explains those budget semantics\n- final item-page title verification supports the normal Vinted selector plus `main h1` / `h1` fallbacks and gives useful diagnostics on failure\n- known unavailable listing pages are classified separately and persisted as `UNAVAILABLE`\n- final verification can inspect up to 20 candidates until it finds enough verified candidates for the current run, preventing stale historical entries from starving valid listings behind them\n- clear catalog/URL/detail target mismatches are persisted as `SKIPPED_TARGET_MISMATCH` so they stop polluting the DISCOVERED backlog\n- transient verification errors remain DISCOVERED and are retried later while processing continues with later candidates\n- target changes requeue prior `SKIPPED_TARGET_MISMATCH` listings; Vinted account identity changes requeue `SKIPPED_CANNOT_NEGOTIATE`\n- plain S25 now explicitly rejects the `Edge` variant, with a regression test\n- adds Flyway V27 for the new target-mismatch status\n\n## Safety\n- real-action preflight remains enabled\n- persistent FIRST_OFFER/NEXT_STEP guard remains enabled\n- quota is still reserved immediately before a real submit\n- ambiguous post-submit failures remain fail-closed\n- per-run real-offer limit remains enforced (default 3)\n- exhausted actual daily quota still blocks new offers\n- transient live-verification problems do not permanently discard a listing\n\n## Tests\n- capacity uses actual remaining quota without future-step reservations\n- exhausted quota returns zero capacity\n- missing negotiation steps fail closed\n- configured bot daily budget is reflected in quota limit/remaining values\n- S25 Edge is rejected as a different variant while normal S25/SM product-code cases stay valid",
